# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES/ADR-053 §2 D5 — THE VAULT EXIT IS OFFERED TO EVERY MEMBER
# `PageLive` decides whether to render the "Move out of the vault" control from `can_declassify?/2`:
# the tenant plane (never the operator one) AND an admin-rank membership role, derived through
# `Samen.Web.TenantRole.admin_scope/2` — the ONE helper that answers "what does this principal
# actually hold in this org?", never `Mount.scope/2`'s fabricated `:member`. This patch drops the
# role half, so on an ARMED host every member is shown a 🔓 button on a vaulted block and the
# reason form to go with it: the surface advertises a governance action the member cannot perform.
#
# Aimed at the SURFACE's gate only. The model's `RoleAtLeast :admin` policy, the tenant-plane
# refusal, the blank-reason refusal and the audit writer are untouched — so a member's crafted
# `declassify_block` event is still refused and the row stays vaulted. The defect is the OFFERED
# affordance (the page's posture), which is exactly what the failing assertion reads.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_declassify_ui_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a member is never OFFERED the control
# MUST_FAIL: the same armed route offers a REAL non-admin member nothing
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/page_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/page_live.ex
@@ -863,4 +863,3 @@
   defp can_declassify?(%Mount{} = mount, org_id) when is_binary(org_id) do
-    writable?(mount) and
-      Samen.Scope.Role.at_least?(TenantRole.admin_scope(mount, org_id).actor.role, :admin)
+    writable?(mount)
   end
